rted by 37.1% of respondents; 60.5% reported 7-9 hours of sleep, and 2.4% reported >9 hours. Among U.S. adults, 13.5% reported three or more sleep-related difficulties.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":507,"renderedHeight":375,"naturalWidth":507,"naturalHeight":375,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 485 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":9563},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6008a3f2.gif","alt":"The figure shows the age-adjusted prevalence of adults aged ≥20 years reporting sleep-related difficulty carrying out selected activities, by usual sleep duration in the United States from 2005-2008, according to the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey. Among adults who reported <7 hours of sleep, the prevalence of each of the six sleep-related difficulties was higher compared with adults who reported 7-9 hours of sleep. For both groups, the most common sleep-related difficulty was concentrating, which was reported by 19.4% of respondents who received 7-9 hours of sleep, but 29.3% of those who received <7 hours of sleep per night.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":615,"renderedHeight":397,"naturalWidth":615,"naturalHeight":397,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 651 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":20095},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_word.gif","alt":"Micros